  "points": 4,
  "timeMinutes": null,
  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "When a positive integer $n$ is divided by 6, the remainder is 5. What is the remainder when $n^2$ is divided by 12?",
  "image": null,
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "1"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "4"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "6"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "13"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "none of the previous"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "A",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Algebra",
    "body": "Write $n = 6k + 5$. Then $n^2 = 36k^2 + 60k + 25 = 12(3k^2 + 5k + 2) + 1$. The remainder is 1.\n\n**Answer: (A) 1**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Try examples",
    "body": "$n = 5$: $25 = 2\\cdot 12 + 1$. $n = 11$: $121 = 10 \\cdot 12 + 1$. $n = 17$: $289 = 24 \\cdot 12 + 1$. Always remainder 1 (and 13 can't be a remainder when dividing by 12).\n\n**Answer: (A) 1**"
   }
  ],
  "topics": [
