  },
  "grade": "11-12",
  "points": 4,
  "timeMinutes": null,
  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "If the difference between $\\angle BOA$ and $\\angle COB$ is $30^\\circ$, what is the value of the angle between the bisector of $\\angle COA$ and the segment $OB$?",
  "image": "qimages/kangaroo/ca-2016-g1112/q20.webp",
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "$30^\\circ$"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "$25^\\circ$"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "$20^\\circ$"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "$15^\\circ$"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "$10^\\circ$"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "D",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Measure from OC",
    "body": "Let $\\angle BOA = \\alpha$ and $\\angle COB = \\beta$ with $\\alpha - \\beta = 30^\\circ$. Then $\\angle COA = \\alpha + \\beta$ and its bisector makes the angle $\\frac{\\alpha + \\beta}{2}$ with $OC$. The ray $OB$ makes the angle $\\beta$ with $OC$. The angle between them is\n$$\\frac{\\alpha + \\beta}{2} - \\beta = \\frac{\\alpha - \\beta}{2} = 15^\\circ.$$\n\n**Answer: (D) $15^\\circ$**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Example",
    "body": "Take $\\angle COB = 30^\\circ$ and $\\angle BOA = 60^\\circ$. Then $\\angle COA = 90^\\circ$, the bisector is at $45^\\circ$ from $OC$, and $OB$ is at $30^\\circ$: the angle between them is $15^\\circ$.\n\n**Answer: (D) $15^\\circ$**"
   }
  ],
  "topics": [
   "geometry"
  ],
