 {
  "id": "kangaroo-ca-2016-g1112-22",
  "bank": "kangaroo",
  "source": {
   "contest": "Canadian Math Kangaroo",
   "paper": "Grade 11-12",
   "year": 2016,
   "url": "https://api.mathkangaroo.ca/api/v1/media/2016/2016gr1112e.pdf",
   "number": 22
  },
  "grade": "11-12",
  "points": 5,
  "timeMinutes": null,
  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "In the picture, the circle touches two sides of square $ABCD$ at points $M$ and $N$. Points $S$ and $T$ lie on the sides of the square so that $|AS| = |CT|$ and $ST$ is tangent to the circle. If the diameter of the circle is 2 and so is $MC$, what is the length of $ST$?",
  "image": "qimages/kangaroo/ca-2016-g1112/q22.webp",
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "$\\sqrt8$"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "$4\\sqrt2 - 2$"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "$2\\sqrt3$"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "3"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "$\\sqrt6 + 1$"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "B",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Coordinates",
    "body": "The circle has radius 1 and touches $DA$ and $DC$, so with $D = (0,0)$ its centre is $(1, 1)$ and $M = (1, 0)$. Since $MC = 2$, the square has side 3: $A = (0,3)$, $B = (3,3)$, $C = (3,0)$.\n\nWith $AS = CT = t$: $S = (t, 3)$ and $T = (3, t)$. The line $ST$ is $x + y = 3 + t$. Tangency means its distance from $(1,1)$ is 1:\n$$\\frac{|1 + 1 - 3 - t|}{\\sqrt2} = \\frac{1 + t}{\\sqrt2} = 1 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; t = \\sqrt2 - 1.$$\nThen $ST = \\sqrt2\\,(3 - t) = \\sqrt2\\,(4 - \\sqrt2) = 4\\sqrt2 - 2$.\n\n**Answer: (B) $4\\sqrt2 - 2$**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Symmetry and the diagonal",
    "body": "Because $AS = CT$, the segment $ST$ is perpendicular to the diagonal $DB$, and the figure is symmetric about $DB$. The circle's centre lies on $DB$ at distance $\\sqrt2$ from $D$, so the point of tangency is on $DB$ at distance $\\sqrt2 + 1$ from $D$. The diagonal has length $3\\sqrt2$, so the tangency point is at distance $3\\sqrt2 - \\sqrt2 - 1 = 2\\sqrt2 - 1$ from $B$. Triangle $SBT$ is right isosceles with height $2\\sqrt2 - 1$ from $B$, so its hypotenuse is $ST = 2(2\\sqrt2 - 1) = 4\\sqrt2 - 2$.\n\n**Answer: (B) $4\\sqrt2 - 2$**"
   }
  ],
  "topics": [
   "geometry"
  ],
  "difficulty": 3,
  "duplicateOf": null,
